      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "10",
          "section": null,
          "quote": "Even \nthough the strengthening effects of SFs may not be as notable as DTs, the \nmassive SFs themselves can still contribute to the work hardening. For \nlow SFE materials with larger separations between the dissociated par -\ntials, SFs afford an effective hardening mechanism for hindering dislo -\ncation motion and preventing recovery mechanisms such as cross-slip at \nelevated temperatures [ 44 ].",
          "table": null,
